    @section ncursesexamplessources Runnable Source Examples

    Run the supplied programs from the source checkout after building/installing the module:
    @verbatim
qore --enable-debug examples/dashboard.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/panels.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/threaded_input.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/forms-inspectors.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/editor-assistance.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/async-review.qr
qore --enable-debug examples/file-attachments.qr
    @endverbatim

    - \c examples/dashboard.qr updates a status display with
      @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawText() "Window::drawText()" and bounded
      @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::readEvent() "Window::readEvent()" calls. Press \c q to exit.
    - \c examples/panels.qr stacks two surfaces with @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel "Panel".
      Press \c t to change which panel is on top and \c q to exit.
    - \c examples/threaded_input.qr runs input in a background thread, shares state through a
      mutex, and joins the reader before closing the session. See @ref ncurses_threads "Threading".

    - @c examples/forms-inspectors.qr submits a validated form into an inspector;
      F2 focuses the inspector, F5 reopens the form, and Ctrl-Q quits.
    - @c examples/editor-assistance.qr requests a worker provider with F1. Type to
      filter, Tab reads documentation, Enter applies an exact edit, and Escape cancels.
      Ctrl-Q quits. The worker posts data; the UI thread applies current responses.
    - @c examples/async-review.qr composes stable approval/decline choices, operation
      progress and a timeline. Enter submits review, C cancels, Enter retries failed or
      cancelled progress, F2/F3 switch progress/history, and Ctrl-Q quits. Completed
      actions cannot accidentally run again. No timing sleeps are used.
    - @c examples/file-attachments.qr demonstrates text/chart previews and unsupported
      media metadata. Space selects, Enter opens an application-provided preview,
      Tab changes pane, E demonstrates export cancellation, F5 starts another selection,
      and Ctrl-Q quits. The example neither reads nor writes the sample paths.

    For an uninstalled build, prefix commands with <tt>QORE_MODULE_DIR=build:qlib</tt>.
    See @ref ncurses_quickstartguide "Quick Start" for terminal setup and
    @ref ncurses_testingguide "Automated Testing" for headless execution.

    @section ncursesexamplespanels Overlapping Panels

    A @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel "Panel" owns a drawable
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel::window() "window" and a position in the stacking order.
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel::top() "Panel::top()" brings it forward;
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel::hide() "Panel::hide()" hides it without discarding its contents.
    Queue panel changes with @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::updatePanels() "Session::updatePanels()"
    and flush them with @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::doupdate() "Session::doupdate()".
    Run this example in a terminal at least 12 rows by 50 columns:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
Ncurses::Panel first(session, 6, 28, 1, 2);
Ncurses::Panel second(session, 6, 28, 3, 10);
first.window().box();
first.window().drawTextInsideLine(0, "First panel");
second.window().box();
second.window().drawTextInsideLine(0, "Second panel");
first.top();
session.updatePanels();
session.doupdate();
session.screen().readEvent();
    @endcode

    For controls inside overlays and modal input routing, use
    @ref NcursesUi::PanelWidget "PanelWidget" and @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget "DialogWidget";
    see @ref ncurses_ui_widgetsguide "UI Widget Toolkit".
*/
